    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q3-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A company decides to give their 23 employees a skills test in order to decide if any of these employees need to be retrained. The maximum possible score in this test is 50 and the results are summarised in an ordered stem and leaf diagram. 0 5 1 9,9 2 1,6,8 where 2 9 = 29 . 3 3,4,5,7 4 2,3,4,4,8,9,9 5 0,0,0,0,0,0\" style=\"--madas-width:565.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q3-question-2.svg\" alt=\"a) Find the median score of the test. ( ) 1 b) Determine the interquartile range of the scores. ( ) 2 The company decides to retrain any employee whose score is less than the lower quartile minus the interquartile range. c) Show clearly that only one employee will undergo retraining. ( ) 2 d) Draw a suitably labelled box plot for this data, clearly indicating any outliers, as found in part (c). ( ) 3 e) Determine with justification the skewness of the scores. ( ) 2\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q3-question-3.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q3-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Looking at the stem-and-leaf diagram: (a) For 23 values the median is observation 12, giving 43 . [A1] (b) The positions of the quartiles are (23 + 1)/4 = 6 and 3(23 + 1)/4 = 18. The sixth and eighteenth observations are 28 and 50, giving IQR = 50 −28 . [M1] [A1] = 22\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q3-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(c) The retraining threshold is 28 −22 = 6. [B1] Only the score 5 is below 6, so exactly one employee is retrained: [A1] (d) Use 19 and 50 for the whiskers after separating the score 5 under the specified rule: [M1] [M1] [A1] (e) The distances to the quartiles from the median are 43 −28 = 15 below and 50 −43 = 7 above: The spread extends much further below the median than above it: [B1] The data are negatively skewed: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 3 is 10 marks.</p>"
