    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-j/q5",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q5-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Bag X contains 3 one pound coins and 2 two pound coins. Bag Y contains 1 one pound coin and 3 two pound coins. A statistical experiment consists of • a coin being picked at random from bag X and placed into bag Y . • then a coin being picked at random from bag Y and placed back into bag X . Find the probability … a) … that a one pound coin will be picked on both occasions in this experiment. ( ) 2 b) … that at the end of the experiment both bags contain £7 . ( ) 2\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q5-question-2.svg\" alt=\"A third coin is picked at random from bag X at the end of the experiment. c) Determine the probability that it will be a two pound coin. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q5-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Drawing a tree diagram:\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The transfer from X changes the mix of coins in Y before the return transfer: (a) The chance of two £1 transfers is (3/5)(2/5) = 6/25 . [M1] [A1] (b) Both bags start with £7, and retain those totals if the transferred coins have the same value. The probability of two £2 transfers is (2/5)(4/5) = 8/25, [B1] so the answer is 6/25 + 8/25 = 14/25 . [A1] (c) The four transfer paths give the following probabilities for the third coin: [M1] Values transferred (pounds) Path probability Conditional chance of a third coin worth £2 1, 1 6/25 2/5 1, 2 9/25 3/5 2, 1 2/25 1/5 2, 2 8/25 2/5\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q5-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"[A1] Multiply each path probability by its final conditional chance: (6/25)(2/5) + (9/25)(3/5) + (2/25)(1/5) + (8/25)(2/5). Sum the products: (12 + 27 + 2 + 16)/125 = 57/125 = 0.456 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 5 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
