    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) From A to B, 102 = 242 + 2a(476), giving a = −0.5 m s−2. [M1] Rearrangement gives 952a = 100 −576 = −476, hence a = −476/952. The deceleration is 0.5 m s−2 . [A1] (b) 10 = 24 −0.5t, [B1] so t = 28 s . [A1] 2a(45)2, [M1] so a = 0.4 m s−2 . [A1] (c) From B to C, 855 = 10(45) + 1 (d) From the preceding displacement equation 405 = 1012.5a, giving a = 405/1012.5. The speed at C is 10 + 0.4(45) = 28 m s−1 . [M1] [A1] (e) Average speed is (476 + 855)/(28 + 45) = 1331/73 ≈18.23 m s−1 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
