      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-j/q16-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) Its speed is √ q 13 km h−1 . (−4)2 + 62 = 2 [M1] [A1] (b) Add t times the velocity to the starting position: f(t) = 18 −4t, g(t) = −5 + 6t . [M1] [A1] (c) At 14:00 the ship is at (10, 7), so the lighthouse has east coordinate 10. [M1] At t = 2, substitute 18 −4(2) = 10, −5 + 6(2) = 7. At t = 3.5, the coordinates become 18 −14 = 4, −5 + 21 = 16. At 15:30 the ship is at (4, 16). For a north-east bearing the lighthouse must have equal positive east and north offsets: [A1] Its east offset is 10 −4 = 6, [A1] so its north coordinate is 16 + 6 = 22. [A1] The position vector is (10i + 22j) km . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
